       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it looks like a dosing error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to 7,650 mg/day. That is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of 2,550 mg (immediate-release). A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day total)\n- **2,550 mg/day total** in some other split, such as 1,000 mg BID or 500 mg TID\n\nWhich one do you want? If the patient is starting metformin, you may also want a lower starting dose, such as 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, titrated up. Once you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter the order."
